# Vendored upstream library versions
#
# Format: <name>   <release-or-tag>   <short-sha>   <full-sha>   <vendored-on>   <url>
#
# This file is the human-readable companion to src/third_party/vendor.json.
# The SHAs below are copied verbatim from the vendor.json `commit_sha`
# fields, which are the source of truth (and are gated by
# tools/check_vendor.py in CI).  tools/vendor_update.py and
# scripts/vendor_update.py rewrite the matching row when a pin is bumped.
#
# The two files describe the same pins, but they do not describe the same
# thing: vendor.json records where each vendor's upstream revision comes
# from, while this file records how the revision is carried in this
# repository:
#
#   - submodule       the sources live in a git submodule; the parent
#                     repository stores a 40-byte gitlink.
#   - checked-in tree the sources are still committed into this repository
#                     (vendor-migration.md Phase 3 pending).  The SHA is
#                     the upstream revision the tree was taken from, not a
#                     description of the tree itself.
#   - fetched         the tree is downloaded at build time and is never
#                     committed (webrtc_audio_processing).
#
# The state of each vendor is spelled out in src/third_party/vendor.json
# (`notes`) and in docs/plan/vendor-migration.md.

