# Patches applied on top of the upstream tree
#
# webrtc_audio_processing is not vendored into git - it is cloned at build
# time by tools/fetch_webrtc_apm.py.  NimRTC's changes to it therefore
# travel as versioned patches in src/third_party/webrtc_audio_processing/
# patches/, applied by tools/apply_webrtc_apm_patches.py:
#
#   0001-cxx20.patch   raise the Meson build to C++20 (required by agc2/*.cc)
#
# Upstream base commit for 0001-cxx20.patch:
#   d0569cfa50c1858ee279d77b3fc8870be6902441
#
# libjuice is still a checked-in tree, and it carries one NimRTC-local
# change on top of the pinned upstream revision:
#
#   src/third_party/libjuice/patches/0001-so-reuseaddr.patch
#       1. src/udp.c no longer sets SO_REUSEADDR/SO_REUSEPORT.  Both
#          let a second bind on an already-bound UDP port succeed, so
#          two ICE agents could end up sharing one UDP port; with
#          SO_REUSEADDR set the kernel ephemeral allocator also handed
#          out duplicate ports to live sockets.
#       2. src/conn_mux.c no longer merges an ephemeral-port request
#          (port_begin == 0 && port_end == 0) into an existing mux
#          registry, so two agents in one process no longer share a
#          single socket and candidate.
#
# Upstream base commit for 0001-so-reuseaddr.patch:
#   77daa8befd828046169adbb012d8de928bfdcdd4
